## Usage

### Basic Usage

```bash
# Process specific subjects with required parameters
python main.py /path/to/bids/dataset 
    --pipeline-name {pipeline_name} 
    --pipeline-id PL001 
    --process-exec-id PE001 
    --bids-filters '{{"subject": ["01", "02"]}}'
```

### Advanced Usage

```bash
# Process specific subjects and tasks with parallel processing
python main.py /path/to/bids/dataset \
    --pipeline-name {pipeline_name} \
    --pipeline-id PL001 \
    --process-exec-id PE002 \
    --bids-filters '{{"subject": ["01", "02"], "task": ["rest"]}}' \
    --max-workers 4

# Disable parallel processing
python main.py /path/to/bids/dataset \
    --pipeline-name {pipeline_name} \
    --pipeline-id PL001 \
    --process-exec-id PE003 \
    --bids-filters '{{"task": ["rest"]}}' \
    --no-parallel

# Overwrite existing outputs with validation
python main.py /path/to/bids/dataset \
    --pipeline-name {pipeline_name} \
    --pipeline-id PL001 \
    --process-exec-id PE004 \
    --bids-filters '{{"subject": ["01"]}}' \
    --pipeline-id PL001 \
    --process-exec-id PE004 \
    --overwrite \
    --validate-bids
```

## Arguments

### Required Arguments
- `bids_root`: Path to BIDS root directory
- `--pipeline-name`: Name of the processing pipeline (used for output path generation)
- `--bids-filters`: BIDS filters as JSON string for file selection
- `--pipeline-id`: Unique pipeline identifier for provenance tracking
- `--process-exec-id`: Unique process execution identifier for provenance tracking

### Optional Arguments
- `--derivatives-dir`: Custom derivatives directory name
- `--overwrite`: Overwrite existing files
- `--no-parallel`: Disable parallel processing
- `--max-workers`: Maximum number of parallel workers
- `--validate-bids`: Validate BIDS compliance

