## Container Usage

### Building the Container

```bash
# Build Singularity container
singularity build {process_id}.sif {process_id}.def
```

### Running the Container

```bash
# Run with Singularity
singularity run \
    --bind /path/to/bids:/bids:ro \
    --bind /path/to/output:/output \
    {process_id}.sif \
    /bids \
    --pipeline-name {pipeline_name} \
    --pipeline-id PL001 \
    --process-exec-id PE001 \
    --bids-filters '{{"subject": ["01"]}}' \
    --pipeline-id PL001 \
    --process-exec-id PE001
```

## Output Structure

The pipeline creates outputs in the BIDS derivatives format:

```
derivatives/
└── {pipeline_name}/
    ├── processing_results.csv      # Detailed processing results
    ├── processing_summary.json     # Summary statistics with provenance
    └── sub-<subject>/
        └── [ses-<session>/]
            └── <datatype>/
                ├── <output_files>  # Processing outputs
                └── <sidecar_files> # Metadata JSON files
```

## Metadata

Each output file is accompanied by a JSON sidecar file containing:
- Processing parameters and configuration
- Pipeline ID and Process Execution ID for provenance
- Execution timing and performance metrics
- BIDS entity information
- Function-specific metadata

## Error Handling

The pipeline includes comprehensive error handling:
- Individual file failures don't stop the entire pipeline
- Detailed error messages are logged for debugging
- Processing results include success/failure status for each file
- Summary statistics show overall pipeline performance

